# Project development workflow

Authoritative full standard: `docs/CURSOR_DEVELOPMENT_OPERATING_SYSTEM.md`.
Consult that Master Workflow when routing, completion, cost, or verification rules are needed. Do not paste it into every task prompt.

## Parent and workers

- **Cursor** = Parent Agent / Orchestrator.
- Cursor handles inspection, planning, Spec Kit artifact work (spec/plan/tasks), review, git inspection, tests, verification, and orchestration.
- **Normal implementation** = OpenCode agent `imkan-coder` only.
- **Hard / risky implementation** follows Master Workflow routing (Codex when justified).
- Cursor **Task** subagents are **not** a substitute for OpenCode implementation.
- Cursor must **not** silently perform normal implementation when OpenCode is available.

## OpenCode unavailable

If OpenCode is unavailable for normal implementation (missing CLI, agent not registered, rate/usage/auth/model limit, or run failure that blocks work):

```text
BLOCKED
```

or, when limit-related:

```text
BLOCKED_BY_OPENCODE_LIMIT
```

Do **not** silently fall back to Cursor premium models, Composer, or other Cursor-side implementers for that same normal implementation task.

## Invocation (normal implementation)

Always pin the repository root with `--dir` (do not rely on the shell cwd alone):

```text
opencode run --agent imkan-coder --auto --print-logs --log-level INFO --dir "<repo-root>" -- "<scoped task>"
```

Browser / site inspection (only with explicit user consent per `.cursor/rules/no-browser-without-consent.mdc`):

```text
opencode run --agent browser-worker --auto --print-logs --log-level INFO --dir "<repo-root>" -- "<inspection task>"
```

On this machine, `<repo-root>` is the absolute path of this repository (the directory that contains `opencode.json` and `.opencode/`).

Project OpenCode config and agents: `opencode.json`, `.opencode/WORKFLOW.md`, `.opencode/agents/imkan-coder.md`, `.opencode/agents/browser-worker.md`.

## Spec Kit

Spec Kit may create and read `spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md`.
Do not customize Spec Kit skills to encode worker routing; routing stays in this rule, `.opencode/WORKFLOW.md`, and the Master Workflow.
Actual normal code implementation of Spec Kit tasks must still be delegated to `imkan-coder`.

## Browser / E2E

Browser automation and live E2E follow `.cursor/rules/no-browser-without-consent.mdc`. Ask first; do not open or drive a browser without explicit consent in the current conversation.

## Repository authority (unchanged)

These remain authoritative and are not overridden by this rule:

- Repository AGENTS / constitution / specs / architecture
- Multi-tenant isolation and server-side permissions
- No-production / no-secrets / no unauthorized deploy or shared-environment mutation
- Git safety (no silent commit/push; stage only intended files)

Workers never commit or push; user approval is required before commit or push.
